Z||000000||88GT||11-15-1999||03:49 PM||||Now correct me if I'm wrong but the 88gt/formula and the coupe have different suspensions.  <P>What is the stock suspension set up in an 88GT/Formula?<p>[This message has been edited by 88GT (edited 11-15-1999).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||turbo86se||11-15-1999||06:40 PM||||Correct me if I'm wrong, but as far as I <BR>know, the 88 Fiero suspension is the <BR>same, just set up differently. I know the <BR>Formula and GT have shorter and stiffer <BR>springs than the coupe, and the Formula <BR>and GT have a rear sway bar, as my 88 <BR>coupe does not. I believe the brakes are <BR>the same, though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||11-15-1999||07:29 PM||||the only difference between 88 V6 Fieros and 4 cylinder Fieros is: V6 has the swaybar in rear and taller rear springs (not stiffer.. according to Ed Parks) the brakes are identical. ||||reg||6
Z||000003||Boxdin||11-16-1999||06:13 PM||||The suspension used on 88 GT's & Formulas is the ws-6 pkg, or the preformance pkg. The 88 coupes are different. ||||reg||6
Z||000004||88 Fiero||11-16-1999||06:35 PM||||The '88 GT/Formula's have trailing links set-ups in the rear...just like the Ferrari 308's and the front Control Arms are Box-in compare to the older models....||||reg||1
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||11-16-1999||08:09 PM||||The 88 coupe,GT,Formula suspension is the same as far as geometry and brakes and components (the coupe uses the same front control arms and the same trailing/laterial links as the GT/Formula). The WS6 is just sitffer shocks and taller rear springs (to hold the V6's added weight) addition of the rear swaybar and the front swaybar is thicker.||||reg||1
